        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "f14ea186-cfb6-51b2-a489-74909832ccfe",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 1359,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.45.100:block:2",
          "start": 749
        },
        "quote": "(c) If a petition is submitted to the Department of Public Works asking that streetlights be installed in an existing subdivision containing underground electrical wiring, then the Department of Public Works shall proceed with the streetlight installation in that subdivision; provided, however, that any such petition must bear the signatures of at least 75 percent of the homeowners of the subdivision, and such homeowners must obligate themselves to pay for the costs of the streetlight installation which are above the standard costs for streetlight installation. (Code 1981 § 41-127. Code 1995 § 134-175.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.45.100:block:2#text",
